 The existing PHPDoc is replaced, or added if not found.
 With the `--reset (-R)` option, the existing PHPDocs are ignored, and only the newly found columns/relations are saved as PHPDocs.

+Instead of writing the full PHPDocs to every model file, you can use the `--write-mixin (-M)` option.
+This will still write the full documentation to `_ide_helper_models.php`, but the model files only get a
+`@mixin` tag pointing to a prefixed class in that file, avoiding duplicate class warnings in your IDE while keeping
+your models clean:
+
+```bash
+php artisan ide-helper:models --write-mixin
+```
+
+```php
+/**
+ * App\Models\Post
+ *
+ * @mixin IdeHelperPost
+ */
+```
+
+The helper file uses a prefixed class name (`IdeHelperPost`) instead of the original one, so there is no
+collision with the model class itself:
+
+```php
+namespace App\Models;
+
+/**
+ * App\Models\Post
+ *
+ * @property integer $id
+ * @property integer $author_id
+ * @property string $title
+ * @property string $text
+ * @method static \Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Builder|\App\Models\Post whereTitle($value)
+ * …
+ */
+class IdeHelperPost extends \Eloquent {}
+```
+
 ```bash
 php artisan ide-helper:models "App\Models\Post"
 ```
